---
/**
 * Lab prototype · mylo/two-places — one question, asked in the app and in the
 * lab's Discord server, answered by the same Mylo from the same sources.
 *
 * The two surfaces start apart, angled away from each other on their own
 * planes, and slide together as the section crosses the viewport (`--p`); a
 * thread of light draws from the question on one side to the same question on
 * the other. Under them, the three ways to reach Mylo in Discord.
 *
 * Night Forest styling on both sides: the server side is described in words
 * ("your lab's Discord server") and drawn in the site's own vocabulary, not
 * in Discord's. Static: the two surfaces side by side, flat, thread drawn.
 */
---

<section class="nf-section tp" data-proto="mylo-two-places" aria-labelledby="mylo-two-places-heading" data-progress>
  <div class="nf-wrap">
    <div class="nf-head-center reveal">
      <p class="nf-eyebrow">Ask Mylo</p>
      <h2 id="mylo-two-places-heading" class="nf-h2">The same Mylo, wherever the lab talks</h2>
      <p class="nf-sub">
        Ask in the app, or in your lab's Discord server. It is one Mylo with one view of the lab, so
        the answer and its sources are the same in both places.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="tp-stage" data-pointer>
      <svg class="tp-thread" viewBox="0 0 1000 400" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M300 92 C 430 30, 560 170, 700 96" pathLength="1"></path>
        <circle cx="300" cy="92" r="4"></circle>
        <circle cx="700" cy="96" r="4"></circle>
      </svg>

      <!-- In the app -->
      <article class="tp-plane tp-web" aria-label="Sample: asked in the app">
        <p class="tp-where">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="4" width="14" height="12" rx="2"></rect><path d="M12 4v12"></path></svg>
          In the app
        </p>
        <div class="tp-web-body">
          <p class="tp-q">Does the Okonkwo paper change anything for the Lakeside grant?</p>
          <p class="tp-row">
            <img src="/images/mylo-head-96.webp" alt="" width="24" height="24" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="tp-name">Mylo</span>
            <span class="tp-status">Looked at 3 things</span>
          </p>
          <p class="tp-answer">
            Yes, in one place: it measures grounding falling off as the patient population drifts
            <span class="tp-pill" title="Source 1: the paper">1</span>, the risk Lakeside lists under what
            blocks it <span class="tp-pill" title="Source 2: the Lakeside project">2</span>. Its sites are all
            academic medical centres, so it says nothing direct about community hospitals.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- In the lab's server -->
      <article class="tp-plane tp-chat" aria-label="Sample: asked in a thread in the lab's Discord server">
        <p class="tp-where">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 5.5h12a1.5 1.5 0 0 1 1.5 1.5v6a1.5 1.5 0 0 1-1.5 1.5H9l-3.5 3v-3H4A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 2.5 13V7A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 4 5.5z"></path></svg>
          In your lab's Discord server
        </p>
        <div class="tp-chan">
          <span class="tp-hash" aria-hidden="true">#</span>clinical-nlp
          <span class="tp-chan-sep" aria-hidden="true">›</span>
          <span class="tp-chan-thread">Okonkwo and Lakeside</span>
        </div>

        <ol class="tp-msgs">
          <li class="tp-msg">
            <span class="tp-av tp-av-a" aria-hidden="true">DR</span>
            <div>
              <p class="tp-by">Dana R. <time>9:12</time></p>
              <p><span class="tp-at">@Mylo</span> does the Okonkwo paper change anything for the Lakeside grant?</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="tp-msg tp-mylo">
            <img class="tp-av" src="/images/mylo-head-96.webp" alt="" width="32" height="32" loading="lazy" />
            <div>
              <p class="tp-by">Mylo <span class="tp-reply">replying to Dana R.</span></p>
              <p>
                Yes, in one place: it measures grounding falling off as the patient population drifts
                (<span class="tp-link">the paper</span>), the risk Lakeside lists under what blocks it
                (<span class="tp-link">Lakeside</span>). Its sites are all academic medical centres.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="tp-msg">
            <span class="tp-av tp-av-b" aria-hidden="true">SK</span>
            <div>
              <p class="tp-by">Sam K. <time>9:20</time></p>
              <p><span class="tp-at">@Mylo</span> could we run its harness ourselves?</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="tp-msg tp-mylo">
            <img class="tp-av" src="/images/mylo-head-96.webp" alt="" width="32" height="32" loading="lazy" />
            <div>
              <p class="tp-by">Mylo <span class="tp-reply">replying to Sam K.</span></p>
              <p>It runs on MIMIC-IV, which the lab already has (<span class="tp-link">datasets</span>).</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </article>
    </div>

    <p class="tp-sample">Sample conversation · fictional lab</p>

    <ul class="tp-ways" data-reveal-group data-reveal-step="110">
      <li class="reveal">
        <p class="tp-way-h">In a direct message</p>
        <p>Personal, like your panel in the app. Only you see it.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="reveal">
        <p class="tp-way-h">With an @mention or a reply</p>
        <p>In a channel, mention Mylo or reply to him. Each person keeps their own conversation there.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="reveal">
        <p class="tp-way-h">In a thread</p>
        <p>One shared conversation for everyone in it, each question answered under the person who asked.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .tp {
    overflow: clip;
  }

  .tp-stage {
    --pv: var(--p, 0.6);
    /* 0 apart → 1 together. */
    --e: clamp(0, calc((var(--pv) - 0.12) / 0.38), 1);
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 3rem;
    perspective: 1500px;
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .tp-stage {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 4.5rem;
      align-items: start;
    }
  }

  .tp-thread {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    pointer-events: none;
    overflow: visible;
  }

  .tp-thread path {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--nf-glow);
    stroke-width: 1.6;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-dasharray: 1;
    stroke-dashoffset: calc(1 - clamp(0, calc((var(--pv) - 0.3) / 0.25), 1));
    vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke;
    filter: drop-shadow(0 0 6px rgb(184 217 154 / 85%));
    opacity: 0.75;
  }

  .tp-thread circle {
    fill: var(--nf-glow);
    opacity: clamp(0, calc((var(--pv) - 0.3) / 0.25), 1);
    filter: drop-shadow(0 0 6px rgb(184 217 154 / 90%));
  }

  @media (max-width: 899px) {
    .tp-thread {
      display: none;
    }
  }

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------ the planes */

  .tp-plane {
    position: relative;
    min-width: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 1.2rem;
    background: var(--surface);
    box-shadow:
      0 30px 70px rgb(0 0 0 / 45%),
      0 0 0 1px rgb(184 217 154 / 5%) inset;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .tp-web {
      transform:
        translate3d(calc((1 - var(--e)) * -60px + var(--mx, 0) * 6px), 0, calc((1 - var(--e)) * -120px))
        rotateY(calc((1 - var(--e)) * 22deg + var(--mx, 0) * 3deg));
      transform-origin: 100% 50%;
    }

    .tp-chat {
      transform:
        translate3d(calc((1 - var(--e)) * 60px + var(--mx, 0) * 6px), 1.5rem, calc((1 - var(--e)) * -120px))
        rotateY(calc((1 - var(--e)) * -22deg + var(--mx, 0) * 3deg));
      transform-origin: 0 50%;
    }
  }

  .tp-where {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0.65rem 1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--divider);
    background: var(--surface-alt);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .tp-where svg {
    width: 1rem;
    height: 1rem;
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--nf-glow);
    stroke-width: 1.6;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }

  /* --------------------------------------------------------------- the app */

  .tp-web-body {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.8rem;
    padding: 1.1rem 1rem 1.3rem;
  }

  .tp-q {
    justify-self: end;
    max-width: 88%;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0.6rem 0.85rem;
    border-radius: 1rem 1rem 0.3rem 1rem;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-primary) 32%, var(--surface-alt));
    font-size: 0.87rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .tp-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }

  .tp-row img {
    width: 1.55rem;
    height: 1.55rem;
    border-radius: 9999px;
    background: #253021;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px rgb(184 217 154 / 25%);
  }

  .tp-name {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .tp-status {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .tp-answer {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .tp-pill {
    display: inline-grid;
    place-items: center;
    min-width: 1.15rem;
    height: 1.15rem;
    border-radius: 9999px;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-primary) 30%, transparent);
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    vertical-align: 0.12em;
  }

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------ the server */

  .tp-chan {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 0.6rem 1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--divider);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .tp-hash {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .tp-chan-sep {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .tp-chan-thread {
    overflow: hidden;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-weight: 500;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
  }

  .tp-msgs {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.95rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 1rem 1rem 1.2rem;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .tp-msg {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.7rem;
    min-width: 0;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .tp-msg p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Mylo's answers sit under the question they answer. */
  .tp-mylo {
    margin-left: 1.6rem;
    padding-left: 0.8rem;
    border-left: 2px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-primary) 45%, transparent);
  }

  .tp-av {
    display: grid;
    flex: none;
    place-items: center;
    width: 2rem;
    height: 2rem;
    border-radius: 9999px;
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  img.tp-av {
    background: #253021;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px rgb(184 217 154 / 25%);
  }

  .tp-av-a {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--cluster-3, #8da66f) 45%, var(--surface-alt));
  }

  .tp-av-b {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--cluster-5, #c9a35a) 40%, var(--surface-alt));
  }

  .tp-by {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .tp-by time {
    margin-left: 0.35rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .tp-reply {
    margin-left: 0.35rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .tp-at {
    padding: 0 0.2rem;
    border-radius: 0.3rem;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-primary) 28%, transparent);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .tp-link {
    color: var(--nf-glow);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: rgb(184 217 154 / 40%);
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }

  .tp-sample {
    margin: 2.4rem 0 0;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  /* ---------------------------------------------------------- three ways */

  .tp-ways {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    max-width: 62rem;
    margin: 2.5rem auto 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  @media (min-width: 760px) {
    .tp-ways {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      gap: 0;
    }

    .tp-ways li + li {
      border-left: 1px solid var(--divider);
    }
  }

  .tp-ways li {
    padding: 0.4rem 1.4rem;
  }

  .tp-ways p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .tp-ways .tp-way-h {
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
    font-family: "Fraunces", Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .tp-web,
    .tp-chat {
      transform: none !important;
    }
  }
</style>
